WEBVTT

00:04.850 --> 00:13.110
<b>A Playthrough of a Certain DUDE's
VRMMO LIFE</b>

01:31.950 --> 01:35.520
<i>Several days have passed since the 
incident where the potions disappeared.</i>

01:35.520 --> 01:38.640
<i>The world of the game has 
changed, just a bit.</i>

01:40.910 --> 01:44.180
<i>Medicine is no longer 
considered a useless skill.</i>

01:46.320 --> 01:49.770
<i>Learning that the NPCs 
can run out of inventory</i>

01:49.770 --> 01:55.100
<i>caused players to rethink 
the Medicine skill.</i>

01:58.640 --> 02:01.400
<i>Now, what to do today?</i>

02:04.020 --> 02:05.470
Hey, Earth.

02:05.470 --> 02:09.430
Hey, Zwei. I hadn't realized 
you were a guild master.

02:09.430 --> 02:11.530
Thanks for the invite!

02:11.530 --> 02:15.690
Sure. These are the members of Blue Color.

02:15.690 --> 02:18.120
Hm... you know Millie, right?

02:18.120 --> 02:19.620
Hi there!

02:19.620 --> 02:22.150
I'll introduce myself first, then.

02:23.140 --> 02:24.750
I'm Nora.

02:24.750 --> 02:27.370
I mostly do melee combat with short swords.

02:29.330 --> 02:30.320
Earth!

02:31.310 --> 02:37.240
Make sure you don't say words like "flat" 
or "smooth" or "cutting board" around her.

02:38.560 --> 02:40.100
Got it...

02:40.320 --> 02:41.900
I'm Rage!

02:41.900 --> 02:44.540
I'm a tanker, and I use a 
one-handed ax and a shield.

02:44.980 --> 02:47.900
Let me aggro the enemies!

02:48.250 --> 02:50.090
And lastly, there's me.

02:50.090 --> 02:54.560
I'm Kazamine. I'm a swordsman 
who uses a bastard sword.

02:54.560 --> 02:56.940
I'm Earth. My weapon is...

02:56.940 --> 02:59.150
I know your weapon! You're an archer, right?

02:59.150 --> 03:01.470
Everybody's talking about you.

03:02.490 --> 03:03.800
'Cause of this!

03:06.160 --> 03:12.290
<b>How can he win with such a crap weapon?</b>

03:07.450 --> 03:11.790
<b>That chef is super-strong.</b>

03:09.080 --> 03:12.540
<b>FYI for anyone watching, bows are super hard to use</b>

03:12.610 --> 03:15.660
<i>I guess I really stood out for that, but...</i>

03:15.660 --> 03:20.060
<i>He was just a low-skill player. 
I didn't want to stand out like that.</i>

03:20.500 --> 03:25.010
Okay, I guess I don't need to 
introduce myself then, but... um...

03:25.870 --> 03:26.720
What's wrong?

03:27.020 --> 03:32.460
Four melee fighters, 
one mage, and an archer...

03:32.460 --> 03:34.940
That's not a very well-balanced party, right?

03:34.940 --> 03:38.220
Millie can use more than one element.

03:38.220 --> 03:40.860
And I can use healing magic.

03:40.860 --> 03:42.140
I see.

03:42.140 --> 03:45.180
So you can fight at melee range 
and also provide support.

03:45.180 --> 03:46.030
Yup.

03:46.030 --> 03:48.680
So, what's our target for the day?

03:48.680 --> 03:51.180
We're going after a Wild Bear.

03:51.180 --> 03:55.330
A Wild Bear? That's a tough opponent.

03:55.330 --> 03:58.560
Well, we're strong enough 
that I think we can take it.

03:59.430 --> 04:03.140
<i>Where is that confidence coming from?</i>

04:04.300 --> 04:06.710
'Cause we've got you, Earth!

04:06.710 --> 04:08.090
You're expecting me to win for you?

04:08.090 --> 04:08.860
Yup!

04:08.860 --> 04:10.320
Don't agree with him!

04:11.020 --> 04:13.680
I've never fought a Wild Bear.

04:13.680 --> 04:19.190
I heard they're fast and smart, 
and really hard to beat.

04:20.470 --> 04:25.100
And when we're done, 
Earth will cook something delicious for us all!

04:25.100 --> 04:26.000
Yup!

04:26.000 --> 04:27.250
I'm cooking, too?!

04:27.250 --> 04:29.880
Is everybody ready, then?

04:29.880 --> 04:31.510
Let's get going!

04:31.510 --> 04:33.130
Yeah!

04:33.770 --> 04:36.180
Were you even listening?

04:36.670 --> 04:40.670
<b>Episode 2</b>

04:36.670 --> 04:40.670
<b>Earth Joins His First Party</b>

04:55.650 --> 04:57.620
Well? See any?

04:57.620 --> 05:02.510
Yeah. I do... But most 
of them are in groups.

05:04.190 --> 05:06.080
There's one in front of us that's by itself.

05:06.080 --> 05:07.490
Let's pull it!

05:07.490 --> 05:11.900
Okay, we'll lure it to someplace 
where we have the advantage.

05:12.170 --> 05:14.830
Long-Distance Vision's very handy, isn't it?

05:14.830 --> 05:17.960
I'm glad we had Earth come with us.

05:17.960 --> 05:18.550
Yeah.

05:18.550 --> 05:21.060
See? He's really helpful, right?

05:21.060 --> 05:23.530
You don't get to brag about me.

05:23.530 --> 05:26.110
Millie, buffs.

05:26.110 --> 05:27.420
Okay!

05:27.760 --> 05:30.910
Aqua Ayuda Anima!

05:34.180 --> 05:37.450
I'm going to split off from the 
group and use my Sneak skill.

05:37.450 --> 05:38.180
Okay.

05:45.820 --> 05:47.390
Hawk Shot!

05:51.060 --> 05:53.260
Confirmed hit!

05:56.340 --> 05:57.580
It's c-coming!

05:57.580 --> 05:58.990
I'm on it!

05:58.990 --> 06:01.080
I'll taunt it!

06:01.080 --> 06:05.330
Activating Aggro Control art "Taunt!"

06:05.880 --> 06:07.510
<b>Taunt</b>

06:10.380 --> 06:11.580
<i>During combat,</i>

06:11.580 --> 06:16.120
<i>monsters have a hidden parameter called 
"aggro" that shows who they're angry at.</i>

06:16.120 --> 06:18.870
<i>Rage is a tank with a high defense,</i>

06:18.870 --> 06:23.850
<i>so he'll direct the enemy's anger 
towards him, and protect us.</i>

06:19.680 --> 06:20.840
Over here!

06:24.220 --> 06:28.000
<i>And while he's doing that, I'll aim 
at the monster from a safe place!</i>

06:33.520 --> 06:35.620
El Re Cura Per!

06:35.620 --> 06:36.940
Light Healing!

06:38.110 --> 06:39.900
Thanks, Millie!

06:39.900 --> 06:42.030
Don't you dare drop aggro on me!

06:42.330 --> 06:44.340
Art: Backstab!

06:43.790 --> 06:44.750
<b>Backstab</b>

06:46.090 --> 06:49.470
Its skin is too tough! 
My short sword can't penetrate it!

06:50.410 --> 06:51.800
It is tough!

06:53.410 --> 06:55.710
I'll fire off a spell, too!

06:55.710 --> 06:59.350
Aster Es Flamma! Fire Lance!

06:59.390 --> 07:01.520
<b>Fire Lance</b>

07:06.340 --> 07:07.270
<i>Uh-oh.</i>

07:07.270 --> 07:09.930
I'm not done with you yet!

07:09.930 --> 07:11.680
Activating Taunt!

07:17.080 --> 07:18.920
El Lebertelle!

07:18.920 --> 07:20.210
Aqua Cure!

07:19.960 --> 07:21.250
<b>Aqua Cure</b>

07:22.710 --> 07:24.550
I didn't think it would be this tough...

07:25.720 --> 07:27.960
<i>I guess I underestimated it...</i>

07:28.520 --> 07:30.590
I think I'm running low on MP!

07:30.870 --> 07:32.810
<i>This is turning bad, fast!</i>

07:32.810 --> 07:36.050
<i>I need to make a quick, decisive call!</i>

07:36.050 --> 07:41.510
<i>I'll believe in my 38 years of life 
experience, and make a risky bet!</i>

07:42.130 --> 07:45.590
<i>I'll aim right between its eyes, 
which is probably its weak spot!</i>

07:43.600 --> 07:48.560
<i>I've got just one chance.</i>

07:48.560 --> 07:51.530
<i>If I can't pull this off, 
then I don't belong in this party!</i>

07:56.430 --> 07:57.550
Did I get it?

08:00.450 --> 08:01.600
What?

08:01.600 --> 08:04.030
I was sure I hit its weak point!

08:04.030 --> 08:05.370
Did I not do enough damage?

08:06.790 --> 08:09.790
Oh, no... We'll all be wiped out!

08:09.790 --> 08:12.090
Damn it! Come get me!

08:13.100 --> 08:14.790
How much HP does it have?

08:15.480 --> 08:18.130
<i>I'll have to play...</i>

08:18.130 --> 08:18.730
<i>my final card!</i>

08:18.730 --> 08:19.240
Hey!

08:19.240 --> 08:20.070
Earth!

08:20.300 --> 08:21.930
Secare Ventus!

08:21.930 --> 08:23.630
Wind Booster!

08:24.190 --> 08:27.330
<i>The spell I learned at 
Wind Magic level 15...</i>

08:27.330 --> 08:29.040
<i>For just 10 seconds...</i>

08:29.560 --> 08:32.490
<i>It gives a huge boost to move speed!</i>

08:32.490 --> 08:34.630
Take this!

08:36.580 --> 08:38.320
Millie! Finish it!

08:38.320 --> 08:42.180
Aster Es Flamma! Fire Lance!

08:51.740 --> 08:53.890
We finally got it, huh?

08:55.240 --> 08:57.650
Honestly, that was tough.

08:57.650 --> 08:58.990
Zwei...

08:58.990 --> 09:02.860
I'm sorry. I didn't think 
it would be this bad.

09:02.860 --> 09:04.740
Now, now...

09:04.740 --> 09:07.220
Let's have something to eat.

09:07.220 --> 09:09.310
I brought a new dish we can all try.

09:09.310 --> 09:11.110
I've been waiting for this!

09:17.160 --> 09:20.120
<b>[Wolf Kabob]
Effect: Move Speed Boost (Long Duration) Score: 8</b>

09:20.930 --> 09:22.610
This is great.

09:22.610 --> 09:25.590
I'm happy 'cause I love meat!

09:25.590 --> 09:29.780
It just looks like meat on a stick, but you 
spent a long time preparing this, didn't you?

09:29.780 --> 09:33.800
The lemon juice brings 
out a nice clean flavor,

09:33.800 --> 09:37.340
and the smell of the herbs 
gets rid of the gamy taste!

09:37.340 --> 09:39.870
How come I just get bread from the market?!

09:39.870 --> 09:43.610
'Cause you love comedy, Zwei. 
I figured you'd see the humor in it.

09:43.610 --> 09:45.840
I do not!

09:45.840 --> 09:47.760
Oh, fine.

09:47.760 --> 09:50.540
Now that the joke's over...

09:50.540 --> 09:52.070
Yay!

09:52.340 --> 09:55.810
Hey, Earth, are recipes 
for cooking expensive?

09:55.810 --> 09:59.710
I wouldn't say expensive... 
you just can't buy them.

09:59.710 --> 10:01.270
Huh? Why not?

10:01.560 --> 10:06.940
There's this unspoken rule among 
crafters that you don't trade recipes.

10:08.550 --> 10:10.370
And why is that?

10:10.370 --> 10:15.670
One reason is that coming up with a 
recipe takes a ton of time and money.

10:16.010 --> 10:19.370
And the second reason is that two 
people making the same recipe

10:19.370 --> 10:22.080
can end up with products of 
wildly different quality.

10:22.520 --> 10:25.140
Even with the same ingredients?

10:25.140 --> 10:26.320
Yes.

10:26.320 --> 10:29.870
Recipes are the product of the hard work 
and creativity of the people who made them.

10:29.870 --> 10:34.130
You can copy the recipe itself, 
but you can't copy the quality.

10:34.130 --> 10:36.560
That's the conclusion 
everyone came to, I guess.

10:36.560 --> 10:38.140
I see.

10:38.140 --> 10:42.500
So even if I bought the recipe for
 these yummy kabobs from you,

10:42.500 --> 10:44.620
I wouldn't be able to make them?

10:44.620 --> 10:47.290
Yes, that's what it means.

10:48.140 --> 10:52.130
Then, from now on, let's have 
Earth cook for us for really cheap!

10:52.130 --> 10:54.560
Hey, where did <i>that</i> come from?

10:54.560 --> 10:58.630
Everybody, you're all really glad 
Earth joined our party, right?

10:58.630 --> 11:00.210
Yup!

11:00.210 --> 11:02.130
Listen to me!

11:02.130 --> 11:04.820
All right, now that that's settled,

11:04.820 --> 11:06.850
I think that's enough 
adventuring for one day!

11:06.850 --> 11:08.140
Yup!

11:08.140 --> 11:09.880
Let's head back, everyone!

11:09.880 --> 11:11.430
Yup!

11:11.430 --> 11:13.070
Listen to me...

11:13.520 --> 11:14.360
<b>Friend List</b>

11:13.520 --> 11:14.360
<b>Add Friend</b>

11:14.620 --> 11:17.080
Earth, can I send a friend request?

11:17.080 --> 11:18.190
Me, too!

11:18.190 --> 11:20.040
I'd like to send one, as well.

11:20.040 --> 11:24.890
<i>My first adventure with a party 
in this world was a success!</i>

11:27.800 --> 11:30.780
I screwed up!

11:30.780 --> 11:33.370
<i>As for how this happened...</i>

11:36.950 --> 11:38.490
Okay!

11:43.050 --> 11:45.550
The forest in the fifth area, huh?

11:45.550 --> 11:47.800
I think I'm ready for it!

12:03.440 --> 12:04.770
Crap!

12:04.770 --> 12:07.480
That's a rock ant with a link ability!

12:07.480 --> 12:09.380
It's going to call its buddies!

12:14.530 --> 12:18.000
I've got no choice but to fight!

12:23.250 --> 12:25.710
It reflects damage, too?

12:26.450 --> 12:27.930
I can't move!

12:30.470 --> 12:33.170
M-My body's going numb!

12:35.580 --> 12:37.890
I'm doomed!

12:42.270 --> 12:47.570
<i>And thus, I took a penalty from 
dying and was warped back to town.</i>

12:49.690 --> 12:54.500
<i>I got my butt kicked, but it's 
my fault for being arrogant.</i>

12:54.500 --> 12:56.560
<i>I'll just have to do better next time.</i>

12:58.860 --> 13:00.690
<i>First update?</i>

13:01.130 --> 13:10.600
A Message to Our Players
This is an important message for all players of One More Free Life Online.
 Some time has passed since the service launch, and we've seen that
all of you are settling into your new lives.
 Thus, we've decided it's time to move onto the next step.
 We will shortly be performing our first major update.
 The update title is "The Fairy Ball".
 In addition to new arts and skills, we will be adding in new items
for crafters as well as fairies that will support you in your adventures.
 These fairies will fight alongside you and help you craft.
They excel at supporting you in your lives here.
 Fairies also have rarities, in the following order: common, uncommon, rare, high rare.
 Please see our official homepage, where we will be making
regular announcements, for more information.
 Please look forward to the update and event.
 One More Free Life Online Operations Team

13:02.210 --> 13:10.070
This is an important message for all 
players of One More Free Life Online...

13:11.130 --> 13:17.490
<i>The message was about a major update 
that was coming called "The Fairy Ball."</i>

13:17.910 --> 13:23.400
<i>There would be new skills and arts, 
more items to craft...</i>

13:23.670 --> 13:29.690
<i>And also fairies who could 
support us as we played!</i>

13:31.830 --> 13:33.620
<i>Hey, this is...</i>

13:33.620 --> 13:38.750
<i>This is definitely gonna be a 
"brawl," not a "ball," right?</i>

13:38.750 --> 13:41.170
<b>Ball</b>

13:38.750 --> 13:41.170
<b>Brawl</b>

13:41.170 --> 13:45.380
<i>The other players are going to 
be leveling up, too, though.</i>

13:45.380 --> 13:47.970
<i>I can't get hit with any 
more penalties from dying.</i>

13:50.670 --> 13:55.810
<i>I worked my way out from under the
 heavy penalty, and learned blacksmithing.</i>

13:55.810 --> 14:00.100
<i>I decided to make an arrowhead that 
could pierce the rock ant's skin.</i>

14:00.950 --> 14:03.700
<i>First, I got two types of iron.</i>

14:04.220 --> 14:09.110
<i>One was basic iron for piercing.</i>

14:09.110 --> 14:11.710
<i>The second was intended 
as a bludgeoning weapon.</i>

14:11.710 --> 14:14.100
<i>I used a purer form of iron for that.</i>

14:15.010 --> 14:19.870
<i>I used the most popular shape, a 
triangular pyramid with indentations on the back.</i>

14:16.540 --> 14:27.470
<b>[Iron Arrowhead]
By attaching this to a Wooden Arrow,
you can create an Iron Arrow.
Effect: Additional Atk + 6</b>

14:20.950 --> 14:27.460
<i>Adding this iron arrowhead to a wooden arrow 
creates an iron arrow with 7 attack.</i>

14:31.120 --> 14:35.440
<i>Then I made a mace-like 
arrowhead out of purer iron.</i>

14:32.760 --> 14:35.680
<b>[Heavy Blunt Arrowhead]
 By attaching this to a Wooden Arrow,
you can create a Heavy Blunt Arrow.
 Additional Atk +8</b>

14:35.990 --> 14:40.030
<i>I think these are all 
the items I want for now.</i>

14:41.890 --> 14:45.030
<i>Now I need something to 
help with my kicks.</i>

14:45.030 --> 14:50.650
<i>I'll probably see other monsters that 
reflect kick damage, like the rock ant.</i>

14:51.150 --> 14:55.700
<i>And kicking doesn't let you 
equip a weapon, so it's weak.</i>

14:55.700 --> 14:58.220
<i>To solve these two problems...</i>

14:59.590 --> 15:03.350
<i>I'll add seven thick, short spikes 
to the bottom of my boots.</i>

15:03.350 --> 15:06.510
<i>And maybe a blade on the side?</i>

15:07.080 --> 15:10.530
<i>What shape should the blade take?</i>

15:10.530 --> 15:14.810
<i>I could base it off a
 kukri knife or a jambiya...</i>

15:17.190 --> 15:18.850
<i>Like this, maybe?</i>

15:19.160 --> 15:21.200
What are you going to do with that?

15:21.890 --> 15:24.450
Just you wait and see, Blacks!

15:24.450 --> 15:27.690
I can't even imagine what 
you'd use it for, though.

15:28.860 --> 15:33.700
<b>[Prototype Leg Blade]
Effect: Atk+12  Additional Defense +2
Special Effect: Reduces reflect damage from kick.
Increases weight.</b>

15:28.930 --> 15:30.200
It's done.

15:33.990 --> 15:36.320
So this is the finished product, huh?

15:36.320 --> 15:37.790
For now, yeah.

15:37.790 --> 15:39.080
But...

15:39.620 --> 15:43.330
I've still got to actually use it if 
I want to know how it can be improved.

15:43.330 --> 15:46.440
I've never seen anyone make an 
item that helps with kicks.

15:46.440 --> 15:47.860
Cool, huh?

15:47.860 --> 15:49.380
Look at that!

15:51.560 --> 15:53.230
Brutal, huh?

15:53.230 --> 15:55.130
The weapon of a weirdo!

15:55.130 --> 15:57.460
Are they boots or weapons?

15:58.520 --> 15:59.780
They're both!

15:59.780 --> 16:01.830
That's such a cool idea!

16:01.830 --> 16:03.200
Right?

16:08.780 --> 16:10.600
Okay, here you go!

16:13.740 --> 16:16.860
Those are some scary-looking 
shoes you've got there.

16:16.860 --> 16:18.270
Are you going to cut something with them?

16:18.270 --> 16:22.110
Oh, these are more for 
shaving down than cutting.

16:22.110 --> 16:24.930
That's even more brutal!

16:24.930 --> 16:26.540
And I thought you were just a chef!

16:27.790 --> 16:30.800
I don't have a choice, Myun!
I need them!

16:30.800 --> 16:33.370
Thanks for the bowstrings. Bye!

16:34.090 --> 16:35.830
<i>Now for my bow...</i>

16:35.830 --> 16:41.240
<i>My Archery level has reached 30, 
so I guess I'll specialize.</i>

16:42.280 --> 16:47.480
<i>I have three choices: 
Shortbow, longbow, and hunting bow.</i>

16:47.930 --> 16:51.250
<i>Shortbows are easy to use, 
but they have a limited range.</i>

16:51.250 --> 16:54.570
<i>They're not good for me, 
since I'm not a melee fighter.</i>

16:54.880 --> 16:59.800
<i>Longbows have range and power, 
but take a long time to fire.</i>

16:59.800 --> 17:01.530
<i>They're not good for solo players.</i>

17:01.940 --> 17:05.510
<i>Which means I should
 probably pick the hunting bow,</i>

17:05.510 --> 17:08.970
<i>since it's got the same range and 
power as what I've been using.</i>

17:09.960 --> 17:13.720
<b>Earth used 3 Exp Points
to specialize his Lv 30 Archery Skill
into Lv 1 Hunting Bow!</b>

17:13.720 --> 17:18.140
<i>It's a more powerful skill,
 so I'll get more of an attack bonus.</i>

17:18.560 --> 17:21.340
<i>Okay, time to get to work on the bow!</i>

17:25.270 --> 17:27.140
I like it!

17:35.040 --> 17:37.270
Making something again?

17:38.410 --> 17:40.530
Yeah. A bow.

17:40.530 --> 17:42.080
That's your bow?

17:42.080 --> 17:44.990
That ain't like any bow I've ever seen.

17:46.350 --> 17:50.530
It's fun to make things that couldn't 
possibly exist in the real world.

17:50.530 --> 17:51.690
Yeah.

17:51.690 --> 17:54.650
That's the best part of 
being a craftsperson, right?

17:55.710 --> 17:57.640
Okay, it's done!

17:58.260 --> 18:02.180
<b>X-type compound hunting bow
Effect: Atk+32</b>

17:58.390 --> 18:01.480
I'll call it the X-type 
compound hunting bow!

18:02.520 --> 18:06.020
It needs more strength to 
pull than my old bow, but...

18:07.440 --> 18:08.940
Okay!

18:08.940 --> 18:10.560
It feels great to fire!

18:10.560 --> 18:13.340
And it's a lot more powerful 
than the last one!

18:24.750 --> 18:26.230
Thanks for everything.

18:26.690 --> 18:28.530
You helped me out a lot.

18:29.510 --> 18:33.320
Tomorrow, I'll try my new one out!

18:50.500 --> 18:53.150
<i>All right, he's not linked to any other ones!</i>

18:55.530 --> 18:57.580
<i>Arrow Twister!</i>

19:02.400 --> 19:03.490
<i>Now!</i>

19:09.400 --> 19:10.840
Heck yeah!

19:20.570 --> 19:22.470
I've got my revenge!

19:23.430 --> 19:27.130
The ant exoskeleton can be used 
for crafting light armor.

19:27.130 --> 19:30.500
Maybe I'll have the armor merchant, 
Myun, take it off my hands.

19:35.020 --> 19:44.950
<b>Attention All Players
 The Fairy Ball is about to begin.
 The first half will involve making
a contract with a fairy.</b>

19:35.520 --> 19:37.760
<i>Attention all players.</i>

19:37.760 --> 19:41.590
<i>The Fairy Ball is about to begin.</i>

19:41.590 --> 19:44.330
<i>The first half will involve 
making a contract with a fairy.</i>

19:49.280 --> 19:51.490
So this is a Contract Crystal, huh?

19:51.830 --> 19:55.940
As an archer, I hope I get to make 
a contract with a wind fairy.

19:56.990 --> 20:00.050
I wonder what I'll get, though?

20:00.050 --> 20:03.140
I don't think there are any monsters here...

20:03.140 --> 20:04.420
Time to try it out!

20:09.340 --> 20:11.270
Fairy contract ritual!

20:26.830 --> 20:27.860
<i>No way...</i>

20:31.350 --> 20:34.660
<i>Hey, Earth, you busy?</i>

20:36.710 --> 20:39.700
What? You failed to make 
a contract with a fairy?

20:43.750 --> 20:44.920
What about you, Zwei?

20:44.920 --> 20:46.720
Oh, I got him.

20:49.120 --> 20:51.060
<i>And everybody else?</i>

20:53.050 --> 20:56.990
I never thought somebody I knew 
would fail to make a contract.

20:58.920 --> 21:02.200
But it's still too early to give up!

21:03.190 --> 21:08.150
The announcement said "first half."

21:08.150 --> 21:11.990
That means there's probably 
a second half, right?

21:13.210 --> 21:15.330
That's true!

21:15.330 --> 21:17.520
And also...

21:18.860 --> 21:23.180
The broken item didn't disappear.

21:23.180 --> 21:27.680
Which means you've got one 
more chance, maybe, right?

21:27.680 --> 21:29.460
That might be right!

21:29.460 --> 21:34.360
I'm sure there's a good chance something 
will happen in the second half!

21:35.270 --> 21:36.270
I see!

21:38.040 --> 21:41.070
I think that's probably right.

21:41.070 --> 21:43.660
But now there's a new mystery.

21:45.200 --> 21:48.660
Why do the fairies like you so much?!

21:50.970 --> 21:52.670
Fairy-playah.

21:52.670 --> 21:53.860
He's a playah.

21:53.860 --> 21:55.510
Indeed, he is a playah.

21:55.510 --> 21:57.100
A playah!

21:57.100 --> 21:58.540
He definitely is!

22:02.030 --> 22:04.410
<i>Fairies sure are cute.</i>

22:04.410 --> 22:07.050
<i>I hope I get another chance.</i>

22:07.470 --> 22:09.930
<b>To be continued</b>
